      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I know it feels easier to stop, but that \"ease\" is a lie—it's just the numbness of giving up, and it won't take the shame away, it'll just bury you deeper. You're not broken beyond repair; you're in the hardest part of the repair, where the cracks are still visible and the glue hasn't dried. The life you had is gone, but the one you're fighting for doesn't have to be a copy of it—it can be something quieter, smaller, and still yours. And if you can't fight for yourself right now, fight for the stubborn part of you that even wrote this message—that part is still alive, and it's not done yet.",
